 "review": {
  "management_type_reason": "MBG・stauden.de・おぎはら楽天（いずれも種）: 花後に花がらを摘む・咲き終わった茎を株元の葉まで切る、秋に茎を切る。種の文だけなので 中。non-invasive と明記",
  "management_type_quote": "Deadhead flowerheads after bloom if self-seeding is unwanted (deadheading may also prolong bloom).",
  "management_type_by_matching": "B 花後刈込型",
  "heat_west_only": "弱",
  "muggy_west_only": null,
  "heat_muggy_west_evidence": "[おぎはら/種] 耐暑性；中\n[おぎはら楽天/種] 耐湿性: 普 通 向きますが高温多湿は嫌います（蒸れ 中 相当）\n[おぎはら楽天/種] 日照 寒冷地: 日向〜明るい半日陰／暖地: 明るい半日陰（西日 × 相当）\n[MBG/種] Best performance occurs in cool summer climates where night temperatures consistently dip below 70F degrees, which unfortunately is a cultural preference that does not fit the profile of a typical St.\n[食い違い] 欧米の文献（種の記述）は 弱 相当。おぎはら植物園の値を採った",
  "spread_evidence": "[こぼれ種 1／MBG・種] In optimum growing conditions, plants will spread by stolons and/or self-seeding in a non-invasive manner to form colonies.\n[地下茎 2／MBG・種] Noteworthy Characteristics Astrantia major , commonly called greater masterwort, is an upright, umbelliferous, stoloniferous, herbaceous perennial (carrot family) that is native to mountain meadows, grasslands, woodland ",
